A region that allocates without end stops the program once the device's
arena reaches its limit, here 64 MiB, instead of filling the GPU's memory.
The program ends although the kernel is still running, waiting for the
host's answer.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/arena-forever.m -o %t.O2
RUN: not %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_DEVICE_ARENA_BYTES=67108864 timeout -k 1 60 %t.O2 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
CHECK: Mercury runtime: the devices' arenas are full: see MERK_DEVICE_ARENA_BYTES
